{"id":27732,"slug":"three-colors-white","title":"Three Colors: White","year":1994,"country":"Poland, France","duration":91,"spine":589,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/27732-three-colors-white","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/release_boxshots/5320-00695df55c45a8bfeb530d06cc667f56/2TjGxYnmDMS7k2liwSXvNrUV1ccY3m_original.jpg","description":"The most playful and also the grittiest film of Krzysztof Kieślowski’s Three Colors trilogy, White follows the adventures of Karol Karol (Zbigniew Zamachowski), a Polish immigrant living in France. The hapless hairdresser opts to leave Paris for his native Warsaw when his wife (Julie Delpy) sues him for divorce (her reason: their marriage was never consummated) and then frames him for arson after setting her own salon ablaze. The film, which goes on to chronicle Karol Karol’s elaborate revenge plot, manages to be both a ticklish dark comedy about the economic inequalities of Eastern and Western Europe and a sublime reverie on twisted love.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Krzysztof Kieślowski","slug":"krzysztof-kieslowski"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Zbigniew Zamachowski","role":"Karol Karol","slug":"zbigniew-zamachowski"},{"actor":"Julie Delpy","role":"Dominique","slug":"julie-delpy"},{"actor":"Janusz Gajos","role":"Mikołaj","slug":"janusz-gajos"},{"actor":"Jerzy Stuhr","role":"Jurek, Karol’s brother","slug":"jerzy-stuhr"},{"actor":"Aleksander Bardini","role":"Notary lawyer","slug":"aleksander-bardini"},{"actor":"Grzegorz Warchol","role":"Elegant man","slug":"grzegorz-warchol"},{"actor":"Cezary Harasimowicz","role":"Inspector","slug":"cezary-harasimowicz"},{"actor":"Jerzy Nowak","role":"Old farmer","slug":"jerzy-nowak"},{"actor":"Cezary Pazura","role":"Money handler","slug":"cezary-pazura"},{"actor":"Jerzy Trela","role":"Karol’s driver","slug":"jerzy-trela"},{"actor":"Piotr Machalica","role":"Tall man","slug":"piotr-machalica"},{"actor":"Teresa Budzisz-Krzyzanowska","role":"Madame Jadwiga","slug":